## Lore

The erta are ugly subterranean predators: a serpentine body with a humanoid upper torso, four human arms, a long spiked tail and a demonic face whose huge lower jaw is lined with jagged teeth. They hunt surface animals and humanoids alike, bursting out of the ground or from among rocks, digging pit traps and starting landslides to catch prey. They are hate-filled and cruel, and enjoy tormenting other creatures.

Their most formidable power is a natural one: they move through rock and earth exactly as the stone masters of Atlantis do. The Splugorth use them for construction, tunnelling and labor, but they are hard to hold, and most enslaved erta have a bio-wizard enslaver implanted in the head. It dulls their speed and alertness but is the only way to keep them from disappearing into the earth. A number of unimpaired erta have escaped and live wild in Atlantis and parts of Eastern Europe, usually alone or in small packs of two to six.

Alignment: any, but generally evil. Weight 500 to 1000 lbs (225 to 450 kg); typically 10 to 20 ft (3 to 6 m) long. Average experience level 1D4+1. Average life span 250 years. Slave market value 50,000 credits wild, 300,000 with an enslaver implanted.

## GM Notes

The book tags the erta an optional player character and monster, and then adds on the same entry that it is not recommended as a player character. Enemies: larger predators, Splugorth minions and humanoids.
